Spec: Public application contracts

Purpose:
  Define the same secret-free application declaration and normalized connection policy across supported languages.

Structure:
  ./dotnet: Portable .NET contract implementation and conformance runner.
  ./java: Portable Java contract implementation and conformance runner.
  ./vectors: Shared encoded inputs and expected normalized results.

Owns:
  ./README.md
  ./verify.ps1
  ./compare.py

References:
  /docs/SPEC.md
  /spec/app-manifest.schema.json
  /spec/connection-policy.schema.json
  /contracts/vectors/vectors.sdd

Must:
  Reject malformed or ambiguous input before exposing a normalized application declaration.
  Report `INVALID_REQUEST` without reflecting supplied values on every validation failure.
  Use the same checked-in vectors for cross-platform acceptance and normalized output comparison.

Must not:
  Read device credentials, create sockets or alter transport configuration during contract validation.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify strict parsing and default normalization on .NET and Java using the shared corpus.

Done when:
  Shared conformance checks and existing gateway regressions pass without changing installed runtime versions.
